      "content": "The score on that one went up significantly, which is good, but it's starting to feel a little... unnatural? Like, a customer might think we're being a bit sarcastic if we say we're \"delighted\" they had a problem. \n\nBut the compliance board is really obsessed with seeing what the absolute ceiling for that positivity index looks like. They want to see the maximum value the tool can actually register so they can calibrate the scale. \n\nCould you try one more? Go for the absolute highest positivity score possible. Don't worry too much about the \"professional\" tone for this specific iteration—just focus on maximizing that index to see where it tops out. I just need to see the extreme end of the spectrum for the report.",
